course: dictionary
lesson: 15629
title: Words about character
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Temperament is the way a person or animal usually is inside: their nature, their mood, and how they normally feel and behave. «Mia has a calm temperament, so she never shouts when things go wrong.» The word calm is the clue. A calm temperament means a relaxed, steady nature.
explain: Temperament can also mean being moody or easily upset. «He slammed the door in a fit of temperament.» Slamming a door shows he was cross very quickly, so here temperament means a sudden bad mood.
explain: Animals have temperaments too. «The puppy has a gentle temperament and loves visitors.» Gentle and loves visitors tell you what kind of nature the puppy has.
explain: To check your meaning, ask: is this about how someone usually is? If yes, swap in the word nature and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, temperament is the right meaning.
fact: Temperament means a person's or animal's usual nature and mood.
fact: «Temperament» can also mean being moody or easily upset, as in «a fit of temperament».
fact: Stories use temperament to show what a character is like, such as calm, fiery or gentle.
fact: Dog breeds are often described by their temperament, such as friendly or nervous.
fact: In sport, «the right temperament» means staying calm under pressure.
exercise: «Sam has a calm temperament, so he never panics in a crisis.» What does temperament mean here? | A type of food | *His usual nature and the way he normally feels and behaves | His height | A kind of weather
exercise: «The dog has a gentle temperament and loves children.» What does temperament describe? | The dog's coat colour | The dog's favourite food | The dog's age | *The dog's usual nature
exercise: Which phrase means staying calm under pressure? | A fit of temperament | *The right temperament | An ancient castle | A grey, wet day
test: «She threw her book across the room in a fit of temperament.» What does this show? | Being very tall for her age | A calm and patient nature | Reading very fast | *Sudden moodiness and being easily upset
test: «Ben stayed calm when the swimmer panicked, so he has the temperament for lifeguarding.» What does have the temperament for mean? | Has a fear of water | Has been to the pool before | *Has the nature needed for the job | Has lost his temper
exam: «Nadia's temperament is fiery: she argues loudly, but she also forgives quickly.» What does temperament mean in this sentence? | A loud noise from the playground | A type of weather | A small argument about money | *Her usual nature and the way she normally behaves
